BerkshireAcademy -> Canterbury[label="55.3 (63.81)
05/09", weight="45", tooltip="NEIRA Girls Fours, Berkshire v Canterbury, Greenwich Academy, Lyme/Old Lyme, Sacred Heart			
Distance: 1300 M Conditions: Steady rain; occasional very light tailwind; flat water. Comments: Races alternated with boys' races. Order of racing: 3V, 2V, 1V, 4V. Berkshire hotseated a rower from 3V to 4V. To ensure fair racing, the course was shortened from 1500 M due to aggressive weed growth in the starting area. In 3V race, GA caught a boat-stopping crab just short of the finish. This would not have impacted finish order, but may have increased the margin. Kudos to cox'ns in 1V and 2V for managing tight 5-boat starts.
